{"title":"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Through a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> a line is drawn parallel to the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, dividing the triangle into two equal areas. \nIf the altitude to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152145ccd173f4b905c3affa0dd4513b2e4fc47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac12 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac14\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2-\\sqrt2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{2+\\sqrt2}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"503\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d8d89db467e374f39ce656c99118c31fb0cea5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  point A=(0,0); point B=(10,0); point C=(4,6); point P=(3,6(-sqrt(2)/2+1)); point D,E;  // Triangle ABC draw(A--B--C--A); dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,SW); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,SE); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NW);  // Point P and triangle CDE dot(P); label(&quot;P&quot;,P,N);  pair[] d=intersectionpoints(parallel(P,line(A,B)),(B--C)); D=d[0]; dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE);  pair[] e=intersectionpoints(parallel(P,line(A,B)),(A--C)); E=e[0]; dot(E); label(&quot;E&quot;,E,NW);  draw(D--E);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c80d6aea325b78a3e76be42f373931ed28543fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABDE]=[\\triangle EDC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32ecf884e3cb6d5f2f2a6669047a5d4f1fd31bae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle EDC]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\triangle ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"38\" />. Because the ratio of their areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, we know that the ratio of their side lengths (and thus their altitudes) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/745ea79512151ff148987df8cb6bd0ba5fc31e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" />. Thus, the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/8/da85ce22c2a113653682634c825fcbf7c0f74c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1*\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e937875927e54b8064cf4d8341cfd7842f48780a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} \\parallel \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"22\" />, the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18ce75c8b7558bfb7597c0800a280f52d020b83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"192\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME\" title=\"1959 AHSME\">1959 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1959 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1959\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" ti